tel 1.0 example.org/contact

# A TEL document conforming to the `contact` schema in
# `demo/contact-schema.tel`.
#
# The pragma must be the first non-blank line of the document (§8, ↯/t.1.2), so
# these notes follow it rather than preceding it.
#
# The pragma's schema identifier is a LIRA *bare reference* — a coordinate
# with no `:version` or `:tag` selector. A bare reference is local-only by
# design: it resolves against the local schema cache and never triggers
# network resolution (§8.2, resolution step 4). To make this document
# portable, one would add a selector (`example.org/contact:1.0.0`) or carry
# the BASE-256-encoded schema signature (§8.1 of the TEL Specification, §8
# of the BinTEL Specification).
#
# Multi-token Scalar values (like a full name) use hard-space mode: a hard
# (double) space after the keyword puts the line into hard-space mode, so
# subsequent soft spaces become part of the value.

name  Alice Anderson
email alice@example.org

phone
  country-code 44
  number 020-7946-0100

phone
  country-code 1
  number 415-555-0123

home
  street   221B Baker Street
  city     London
  country  UK

work
  street   1 Acme Way
  city     San Francisco
  country  US

active
